  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   - We represent h(x) as a mixture of N_atoms Gaussians, their centers and widths optimized to minimize the maximum correlation with 1-h(x+k)\n   - This approach allows continuous optimization and can escape discrete local optima\n   - We address the problem's non-convexity by using alternating optimization between centers and widths\n   - Unlike the provided SLSQP implementation, we use Gaussian kernels and continuous space allowing finer search granularity\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Let h(x) = (1/integral) \u2211\u1d62 exp(- (x-centers_i)\u00b2/(2*width_i\u00b2))\n   - Constraints: 0.1 \u2264 centers_i \u2264 1.9 (avoid domain edges)\n   - 1 \u2264 widths_i \u2264 4 (controls pulse spread)\n   - Integral constraint automatically satisfied by final normalization\n   - Objective: C5 = max_k [2.0/n * np.max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full'))]\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   - Initialize parameters: centers uniform in [0.3, 1.7], widths uniform in [1.5, 3.0]\n   - Normalize integral to 1 by factor f = n*0.5 / \u222bh(x)dx\n   - Build evaluation function using np.exp and np.trapz for integrals\n   - Objective: C5 = np.max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')) * 2.0 / n\n   - Optimization:\n     - Gradient descent with LBFGS-B via partial_function()\n     - Update centers with boundaries [0.3,1.7] for each atom\n     - Update widths with boundaries [1.3,4] for each atom\n   - Phase: Start with few atoms (N_atoms=10\u219250\u2192100) then increase if improvement sufficient\n   - Repair function: Clip parameters to bounds, re-normalize integral\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   - Default: 50 atoms, dx=2.0/n\n   - Width hyperparameter: 1.5-3.0 (favors less overlap but may overfit)\n   - Center spacing: minimizes self-overlap by avoiding periodicity\n   - Optimization: use early termination for plateau detection\n   - Atom count: dyn changes if improvement < 0.01*previous for 3 consecutive updates\n\n5. Computation budget:\n   - Initial: N_atoms=50\n   - Time per eval ~ O(n*N_atoms) (replace n=500)\n   - Check boundaries every 10 iterations\n   - Scale runs by available time: if available_time<600, use N_atoms=20\n   - Pre-check integral at start and repair\n   - Global fallback: if optimization fails, fall back to parent solution\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   - Ensure 0\u2264h[i]\u22641: done by clipping\n   - Integral normalization: final adjustment ensures sum(h)*(2/n)\u22481\u00b11e-4\n   - Re-evaluate refined solution with _eval\n   - Requirements check: recompute correlation with original dx\n   - Return (h, C5, n) after parameter repair\n   - Repair function: Integrate for normalization, clip malformed values",
